/-!
# A bound on the ranks at which a module of finite type can be locally free

Let `F` be a quasi-coherent module of finite presentation on an affine scheme `X`. Then `F` is
generated by `c` global sections for some `c`, and therefore, as the proof of Stacks 05UE
records, `dim_{κ(x)}(F_x ⊗ κ(x))` never exceeds `c` at any point `x`. In particular the functor
`H_p` of Stacks 05MP is empty for `p > c`: a rank at which `F`, or any pullback of `F`, is
locally free is at most `c`.

This file proves that bound. The source states it for `F` itself; what the coproduct
decomposition needs is the same bound for every pullback of `F`, which is what is proved here
and is no harder, a pullback of a module generated by `c` sections being generated by `c`
sections.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.rank_le_of_epi_from_free`: if a module is free of rank `r` near a point
  and is the target of an epimorphism from the free module on `I`, then `r ≤ #I`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_rank_bound_of_compactSpace`: **the bound `c` of Stacks 05UE.** A
  module of finite type on a quasi-compact scheme admits a `c` bounding the rank of local
  freeness of every one of its pullbacks, at every point.

## Implementation notes

The bound is read on the stalk. Taking the stalk at a point is a functor from sheaves of
modules to modules over the ring stalk which preserves colimits (Stacks 01AH,
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.stalkFunctor_preservesColimits`), so it carries the free
module on `I` to a module of rank `#I` — the coproduct of `I` copies of the unit module, whose
stalk is the ring stalk itself and so has rank one — and it carries an epimorphism to a
surjection. A surjection does not raise the rank, which is the comparison of cardinalities.

Mathlib's stalk functor for sheaves of modules is valued in modules over the `RingCat`-valued
stalk of the structure sheaf, which carries only a `Ring` instance. Commutativity and
nontriviality, which is what makes the strong rank condition available and hence the rank
comparison meaningful, are transported from the `CommRingCat`-valued stalk — the local ring at
the point — along the comparison isomorphism for the forgetful functor, which preserves the
filtered colimit computing the stalk. This is why the rank computation for free modules lives
inside the proof of `AlgebraicGeometry.free_rank_le_of_epi` rather than being stated on its
own: its statement would have to name those instances.

To apply this to a module that is only locally free near the point, the configuration is
restricted to an open neighbourhood on which the module is free: restriction is a pullback,
which preserves freeness on a fixed index set (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.pullbackFreeIso`)
and, being a left adjoint, preserves epimorphisms.

Quasi-compactness turns the opens carrying the local generators of a module of finite type
into a finite family, and the bound is the largest of their numbers of generators. Near a
point of a pullback, the pullback is a quotient of the free module on the generators of the
member containing the image of that point. Affine schemes are quasi-compact, which covers the
hypothesis of the source.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05UE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05UE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05MP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05MP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01AH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01AH)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-! ### Epimorphisms across the two spellings of the category of modules on a scheme

`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules X` and `SheafOfModules X.ringCatSheaf` are the same type but
not the same term, so an `Epi` hypothesis stated for one is not found by instance search for
the other. The lemmas below take their epimorphism hypotheses as explicit arguments, so the
proofs cross the boundary by passing terms rather than through instance search. For the hom and
the inverse of an isomorphism no local lemma is needed: the Mathlib instances
`CategoryTheory.Iso.isIso_hom` and `CategoryTheory.Iso.isIso_inv` are applied as terms, which
fixes the category instance from the isomorphism, and `CategoryTheory.IsIso.epi_of_iso` is then
read off them by dot notation. -/

/-- A composite of epimorphisms is an epimorphism. -/
private theorem epi_comp' {C : Type*} [Category C] {A B D : C} (a : A ⟶ B) (b : B ⟶ D)
    (ha : Epi a) (hb : Epi b) : Epi (a ≫ b) :=
  have := ha
  have := hb
  inferInstance

/-- Pulling back a module along a morphism of schemes preserves epimorphisms: it is a left
adjoint. -/
private theorem epi_pullback_map {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (g : Y ⟶ X) {M N : X.Modules} (f : M ⟶ N)
    (hf : Epi f) : Epi ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).map f) :=
  have := hf
  inferInstance

/-- An equivalence of categories of modules preserves epimorphisms. -/
private theorem epi_overEquiv_map {X : Scheme.{u}} (U : X.Opens)
    {M N : SheafOfModules.{u} (Sheaf.over X.ringCatSheaf U)} (f : M ⟶ N) (hf : Epi f) :
    Epi ((Scheme.Modules.overEquiv U).functor.map f) :=
  have := hf
  inferInstance

/-- Pulling back an epimorphism along `g` and precomposing with the inverse of an isomorphism
is an epimorphism. -/
private theorem epi_iso_inv_comp_pullback_map {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (g : Y ⟶ X) {M N : X.Modules}
    {A : Y.Modules} (e : (Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj M ≅ A) (f : M ⟶ N) (hf : Epi f) :
    Epi (e.inv ≫ (Scheme.Modules.pullback g).map f) :=
  epi_comp' _ _ e.isIso_inv.epi_of_iso (epi_pullback_map g f hf)

/-! ### An epimorphism of free modules does not raise the index cardinality -/

/-- **The rank comparison on a stalk.** An epimorphism from the free module on `I` to the free
module on `J` forces `#J ≤ #I`.

The stalk at a point is a colimit-preserving functor to modules over the ring stalk, so it
takes the free module on `K` to a module of rank `#K` and the epimorphism to a surjection; a
surjection does not raise the rank. The ring stalk is commutative and nonzero because it is
isomorphic, as a ring, to the local ring at the point, so it satisfies the strong rank
condition. -/
theorem free_rank_le_of_epi {X : Scheme.{u}} (x : X) {I J : Type u}
    (f : SheafOfModules.free.{u} (R := X.ringCatSheaf) I ⟶ SheafOfModules.free.{u} J)
    (hf : Epi f) : Cardinal.mk J ≤ Cardinal.mk I := by
  classical
  have := hf
  let R := ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := RingCat.{u}) (X := X.toTopCat)
    X.ringCatSheaf.obj x)
  let eR : R ≃+* ToType (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
    Iso.ringCatIsoToRingEquiv
      (preservesColimitIso (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})
        ((OpenNhds.inclusion x).op ⋙ X.presheaf)).symm
  let : CommRing R := { (inferInstance : Ring R) with
    mul_comm := fun a b ↦ eR.injective (by simp [mul_comm]) }
  let : Nontrivial R := eR.toEquiv.nontrivial
  let G := SheafOfModules.stalkFunctor X.ringCatSheaf x
  let E := G.obj (SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf)
  let e : E ≃ₗ[R] R := LocallyFreeRank.unitStalkLEquiv X.ringCatSheaf.obj x
  let : Module.Free R E := Module.Free.of_equiv e.symm
  have hrank : ∀ K : Type u, Module.rank R (G.obj (SheafOfModules.free.{u} K))
      = Cardinal.mk K := by
    intro K
    have hc : IsColimit (Cofan.mk (G.obj (SheafOfModules.free.{u} K))
        (fun k ↦ G.map ((SheafOfModules.freeCofan (R := X.ringCatSheaf) K).inj k)) :
          Cofan (fun _ : K ↦ E)) :=
      (Cofan.isColimitMapCoconeEquiv G _ _)
        (isColimitOfPreserves G (SheafOfModules.isColimitFreeCofan K))
    have ei : G.obj (SheafOfModules.free.{u} K) ≅
        ModuleCat.of R (DirectSum K fun _ : K ↦ ToType E) :=
      hc.coconePointUniqueUpToIso (coproductIsCoproduct (fun _ : K ↦ E)) ≪≫
        ModuleCat.coprodIsoDirectSum (fun _ : K ↦ E)
    rw [ei.toLinearEquiv.rank_eq, rank_directSum]
    have hE : Module.rank R E = 1 := e.rank_eq.trans (Module.rank_self R)
    show Cardinal.sum (fun _ : K ↦ Module.rank R E) = Cardinal.mk K
    simp only [hE, Cardinal.sum_const, Cardinal.lift_id, mul_one]
  have hsurj := (ModuleCat.epi_iff_surjective (G.map f)).mp inferInstance
  exact (hrank J).symm.trans_le
    ((LinearMap.rank_le_of_surjective (G.map f).hom hsurj).trans_eq (hrank I))

/-! ### The rank at a point is bounded by the number of generators -/

/-- A module finite locally free of rank `p` is free on the index set `Fin p` on a
neighbourhood of every point. -/
private theorem exists_pullback_iso_free {X : Scheme.{u}} (M : X.Modules) (p : ℕ)
    (hM : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} M p) (x : X) :
    ∃ U : X.Opens, x ∈ U ∧
      Nonempty ((Scheme.Modules.pullback U.ι).obj M ≅
        SheafOfModules.free.{u} (ULift.{u} (Fin p))) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨q, hq, hrank⟩ := hM.exists_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRankData
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := ((Opens.coversTop_iff X q.X).mp q.coversTop).exists_mem x
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := Scheme.Modules.nonempty_restrict_iso_free_of_isLocallyFreeData M q hq i
  refine ⟨q.X i, hi, ⟨?_⟩⟩
  refine ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctorIsoPullback
    (Scheme.Opens.ι (q.X i))).app M).symm ≪≫ e ≪≫ ?_
  exact (SheafOfModules.freeFunctor
      (R := (Scheme.Opens.toScheme (q.X i)).ringCatSheaf)).mapIso
    (((hrank i).some.trans Equiv.ulift.{u, 0}.symm).toIso)

/-- **The rank bound at a point.** If a module on a scheme is free of rank `r` near a point and
is the target of an epimorphism from the free module on `I`, then `r ≤ #I`.

Restricting to a neighbourhood on which the module is free turns the epimorphism into an
epimorphism of free modules, where the comparison is the one read on the stalk. -/
theorem rank_le_of_epi_from_free {X : Scheme.{u}} (M : X.Modules) (x : X) (r : ℕ)
    (h : FreeAtPointOfRank M x r) {I : Type u}
    (f : SheafOfModules.free.{u} (R := X.ringCatSheaf) I ⟶ M) (hf : Epi f) :
    (r : Cardinal.{u}) ≤ Cardinal.mk I := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨U, hxU, hU⟩ := h
  have hU' : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullback U.ι).obj M) r :=
    { exists_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRankData := hU.exists_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRankData }
  obtain ⟨V, hxV, ⟨eV⟩⟩ := exists_pullback_iso_free
    ((Scheme.Modules.pullback U.ι).obj M) r hU' ⟨x, hxU⟩
  have h1 : Epi ((Scheme.Modules.pullback U.ι).map f) := epi_pullback_map U.ι f hf
  have heI : (Scheme.Modules.pullback V.ι).obj
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullback U.ι).obj (SheafOfModules.free.{u} I)) ≅
        SheafOfModules.free.{u} I :=
    (Scheme.Modules.pullback V.ι).mapIso (Scheme.Modules.pullbackFreeIso U.ι I) ≪≫
      Scheme.Modules.pullbackFreeIso V.ι I
  have hle := free_rank_le_of_epi (X := V.toScheme) ⟨⟨x, hxU⟩, hxV⟩
    ((heI.inv ≫ (Scheme.Modules.pullback V.ι).map
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullback U.ι).map f)) ≫ eV.hom)
    (epi_comp' _ _ (epi_iso_inv_comp_pullback_map V.ι heI _ h1) eV.isIso_hom.epi_of_iso)
  simpa using hle

/-! ### The epimorphism from the free module on a family of local generators -/

/-- The free sheaf of modules on an open subscheme `U` is the image of the free sheaf of modules
on the slice site at `U` under the equivalence between the two: the equivalence is a left
adjoint, so it preserves coproducts, and it carries the structure sheaf to the structure sheaf. -/
private noncomputable def freeOverIsoOpen {X : Scheme.{u}} (U : X.Opens) (I : Type u) :
    SheafOfModules.free (R := (U : Scheme.{u}).ringCatSheaf) I ≅
      (Scheme.Modules.overEquiv U).functor.obj
        (SheafOfModules.free (R := X.ringCatSheaf.over U) I) :=
  have hpres : PreservesColimitsOfShape.{u, u} (Discrete I)
      (Scheme.Modules.overEquiv U).functor :=
    Functor.instPreservesColimitsOfShapeOfIsLeftAdjoint.{u, u, u, u + 1, u, u + 1} _
  @SheafOfModules.mapFreeIso _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _
    (Scheme.Modules.overEquiv U).functor I hpres (Iso.refl _)

/-- On an open carrying a family of generating sections, the module is a quotient of the free
module on those generators. -/
private noncomputable def generatorsEpi {X : Scheme.{u}} (M : X.Modules) (U : X.Opens)
    (σ : (M.over U).GeneratingSections.{u}) :
    SheafOfModules.free.{u} (R := U.toScheme.ringCatSheaf) σ.I ⟶
      (Scheme.Modules.pullback U.ι).obj M :=
  (freeOverIsoOpen U σ.I).hom ≫
    (Scheme.Modules.overEquiv U).functor.map σ.π ≫
    ((Scheme.Modules.overFunctorEquiv U).app M).hom ≫
      ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctorIsoPullback U.ι).app M).hom

private theorem epi_generatorsEpi {X : Scheme.{u}} (M : X.Modules) (U : X.Opens)
    (σ : (M.over U).GeneratingSections.{u}) : Epi (generatorsEpi M U σ) :=
  epi_comp' _ _ (freeOverIsoOpen U σ.I).isIso_hom.epi_of_iso
    (epi_comp' _ _ (epi_overEquiv_map U σ.π σ.epi)
      (epi_comp' _ _ ((Scheme.Modules.overFunctorEquiv U).app M).isIso_hom.epi_of_iso
        ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctorIsoPullback U.ι).app M).isIso_hom.epi_of_iso))

/-- At a point of a pullback lying over an open carrying generating sections, the rank of local
freeness is at most the number of those generators. -/
private theorem rank_le_card_generators {X : Scheme.{u}} (M : X.Modules) (U : X.Opens)
    (σ : (M.over U).GeneratingSections.{u}) {Y : Scheme.{u}} (g : Y ⟶ X) (y : Y) (r : ℕ)
    (hiy : g y ∈ U)
    (hr : FreeAtPointOfRank ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj M) y r) :
    (r : Cardinal.{u}) ≤ Cardinal.mk σ.I := by
  classical
  have hcomp : Scheme.Hom.resLE g U (g ⁻¹ᵁ U) le_rfl ≫ U.ι = (g ⁻¹ᵁ U).ι ≫ g :=
    Scheme.Hom.resLE_comp_ι g le_rfl
  have hiso : (Scheme.Modules.pullback (g ⁻¹ᵁ U).ι).obj
        ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj M) ≅
      (Scheme.Modules.pullback (Scheme.Hom.resLE g U (g ⁻¹ᵁ U) le_rfl)).obj
        ((Scheme.Modules.pullback U.ι).obj M) :=
    (Scheme.Modules.pullbackComp (g ⁻¹ᵁ U).ι g).app M ≪≫
      (Scheme.Modules.pullbackCongr hcomp.symm).app M ≪≫
        ((Scheme.Modules.pullbackComp
          (Scheme.Hom.resLE g U (g ⁻¹ᵁ U) le_rfl) U.ι).app M).symm
  have hfree : FreeAtPointOfRank
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (Scheme.Hom.resLE g U (g ⁻¹ᵁ U) le_rfl)).obj
        ((Scheme.Modules.pullback U.ι).obj M))
      (⟨y, hiy⟩ : (g ⁻¹ᵁ U).toScheme) r :=
    freeAtPointOfRank_of_moduleIso hiso
      (freeAtPointOfRank_pullback (g ⁻¹ᵁ U).ι _ ⟨y, hiy⟩ r hr)
  refine rank_le_of_epi_from_free _ (⟨y, hiy⟩ : (g ⁻¹ᵁ U).toScheme) r hfree
    ((Scheme.Modules.pullbackFreeIso
        (Scheme.Hom.resLE g U (g ⁻¹ᵁ U) le_rfl) σ.I).inv ≫
      (Scheme.Modules.pullback
        (Scheme.Hom.resLE g U (g ⁻¹ᵁ U) le_rfl)).map (generatorsEpi M U σ)) ?_
  exact epi_iso_inv_comp_pullback_map _ _ _ (epi_generatorsEpi M U σ)

/-! ### The bound over a quasi-compact scheme, for every pullback -/

/-- The bound at a point of a pullback lying over a member of a family of local generators,
read off that family. -/
private theorem rank_le_card_generators_of_mem {X : Scheme.{u}} (M : X.Modules)
    (q : M.LocalGeneratorsData.{u}) (i : q.I) {Y : Scheme.{u}} (g : Y ⟶ X) (y : Y) (r : ℕ)
    (hiy : g y ∈ q.X i)
    (hr : FreeAtPointOfRank ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj M) y r) :
    (r : Cardinal.{u}) ≤ Cardinal.mk (q.generators i).I :=
  rank_le_card_generators M (q.X i) (q.generators i) g y r hiy hr

/-- A bound on a natural number by the cardinality of a finite type is a bound by its
cardinal count. -/
private theorem le_natCard_of_le_mk {I : Type u} [Finite I] {r : ℕ}
    (h : (r : Cardinal.{u}) ≤ Cardinal.mk I) : r ≤ Nat.card I := by
  classical
  have : Fintype I := Fintype.ofFinite I
  rw [Cardinal.mk_fintype] at h
  rw [Nat.card_eq_fintype_card]
  exact_mod_cast h

/-- Finitely many members of a family of local generators of a module on a quasi-compact scheme
already cover it. -/
private theorem exists_finset_cover_localGenerators {X : Scheme.{u}} [CompactSpace X]
    (M : X.Modules) (q : M.LocalGeneratorsData.{u}) :
    ∃ s : Finset q.I, ∀ x : X, ∃ i ∈ s, x ∈ (q.X i : Set X) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := isCompact_univ.elim_finite_subcover (fun i ↦ (q.X i : Set X))
    (fun i ↦ (q.X i).isOpen) (fun x _ ↦ by
      obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := ((Opens.coversTop_iff X q.X).mp q.coversTop).exists_mem x
      exact Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨i, hi⟩)
  refine ⟨s, fun x ↦ ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨i, hi, hx⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion₂.mp (hs (Set.mem_univ x))
  exact ⟨i, hi, hx⟩

/-- The bound at one point, against a member of the family containing its image. -/
private theorem rank_le_of_mem_cover {X : Scheme.{u}} (M : X.Modules)
    (q : M.LocalGeneratorsData.{u}) (hq : q.IsFiniteType) (i : q.I) (c : ℕ)
    (hc : Nat.card (q.generators i).I ≤ c) {Y : Scheme.{u}} (g : Y ⟶ X) (y : Y) (r : ℕ)
    (hiy : g y ∈ q.X i)
    (hr : FreeAtPointOfRank ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj M) y r) : r ≤ c :=
  have : Finite (q.generators i).I := (hq.isFiniteType i).finite
  (le_natCard_of_le_mk (rank_le_card_generators_of_mem M q i g y r hiy hr)).trans hc

/-- The bound against a finite subfamily of local generators that already covers. -/
private theorem rank_le_of_cover {X : Scheme.{u}} (M : X.Modules)
    (q : M.LocalGeneratorsData.{u}) (hq : q.IsFiniteType) (s : Finset q.I)
    (hs : ∀ x : X, ∃ i ∈ s, x ∈ (q.X i : Set X)) (c : ℕ)
    (hc : ∀ i ∈ s, Nat.card (q.generators i).I ≤ c) (Y : Scheme.{u}) (g : Y ⟶ X) (y : Y)
    (r : ℕ) (hr : FreeAtPointOfRank ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj M) y r) : r ≤ c := by
  obtain ⟨i, hi, hiy⟩ := hs (g y)
  exact rank_le_of_mem_cover M q hq i c (hc i hi) g y r hiy hr

private theorem exists_rank_bound_of_localGenerators {X : Scheme.{u}} [CompactSpace X]
    (M : X.Modules) (q : M.LocalGeneratorsData.{u}) (hq : q.IsFiniteType) :
    ∃ c : ℕ, ∀ (Y : Scheme.{u}) (g : Y ⟶ X) (y : Y) (r : ℕ),
      FreeAtPointOfRank ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj M) y r → r ≤ c :=
  let ⟨s, hs⟩ := exists_finset_cover_localGenerators M q
  ⟨s.sup (fun i ↦ Nat.card (q.generators i).I),
    rank_le_of_cover M q hq s hs _ fun _ hi ↦
      Finset.le_sup (f := fun i ↦ Nat.card (q.generators i).I) hi⟩

/-- **The bound `c` of Stacks Project, Tag 05UE.** A module of finite type on a quasi-compact
scheme admits a natural number `c` such that no pullback of it is free of rank greater than `c`
near any point.

On a quasi-compact scheme finitely many of the opens carrying local generators already cover,
and `c` is the largest of their numbers of generators. -/
theorem exists_rank_bound_of_compactSpace {X : Scheme.{u}} [CompactSpace X] (M : X.Modules)
    [M.IsFiniteType] :
    ∃ c : ℕ, ∀ (Y : Scheme.{u}) (g : Y ⟶ X) (y : Y) (r : ℕ),
      FreeAtPointOfRank ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj M) y r → r ≤ c := by
  obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ := SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.exists_localGeneratorsData M
  exact exists_rank_bound_of_localGenerators M q hq


end AlgebraicGeometry

end
